Maybe I am simply struck again by the language barrier; I am
interpreting the term "conduct" in the Nethack context quite
differently; and I still wouldn't call it a conduct if you're carrying
a quantum chest to the Planes. I'd call it at most a style gimmick,
but I don't even see any style issue there.[*] YMMV.

> And who's to say which conducts & style are "better" than another?

WRT "better"; anyone can say that, especially if he/she qualifies it
as "IMO".

Besides that, conducts (and I mean real conducts) can indeed be valued
by some empirical scale. Wishless or genocideless are easier conducts
than pacifists or naked ascensions (we don't need to re-open that can,
now). You can make up a case to ascend (mostly) itemless as conduct,
and there's room to make it still more difficult by carrying so many
chests and boxes that you are strained. But that simply doesn't make
sense and isn't sane (even if thinking in Nethack categories).

Qualifying something as "stylish", "lacking/bad style", or "has
nothing to do with style", is indeed more difficult. So if one feels
it to be stylish to carry a quantum box to Astral... - suum cuique.
[**] I'd rather call it irrelevant and silly.

But implementing a special case into Nethack for this corner-case,
which was my point, well... I think it's not worth.

